  "caption_draft": "Three protocol choices change what is measured when AI inpainting is scored on museum paintings. (a) Default 8x nearest-neighbour mask downsampling misses part of a 1% crack; a grid-aligned input reaches every hole pixel. (b) At SDXL strength 0.99 the hole's prefill colour shifts luminance bias and error. (c) PowerPaint's safety checker withholds outputs at different rates in two museums. (d) Under the controlled protocol the masked-MAE ordering is the same in both museums, four media and six losses.",
